        "ocr_result": "8\nPEW RESEARCH CENTER\nOther important findings\nVoters pessimistic on how Trump will impact race relations. Nearly half ofvoters (46%) say\nTrump’s election will lead to worse race relations, while only about half as many (25%) expect race\nrelations to improve; 26% say his election won’t make a difference. Among Clinton voters, 84%\nexpect race relations to worsen under Trump. Among Trump supporters, half expect\nimprovement, while 38% say his election won’t makea difference.\nPost-victory, most Trump backers confident in an accurate vote count. ID August, just 38% of\nregistered voters who supported Trump were very confident that their vote would be counted\naccurately. But in the aftermath ofTrump’s\nvictory, 75% expressed confidence that their cs\nvotes were counted accurately. The views of\nWill the country elect a female\nClinton supporters showed no change: After\npresident in your lifetime?\nthe election 67% were confident that their\n% ofvoters who say ...\nvotes were counted accurately.\nNo\nmYes\nAll voters\n17 ol\nMost expect woman president, eventually.\nFollowing Clinton’s defeat, a sizable majority\n—|\nof voters (79%) still expect there will be a\nfemale president “in their lifetime.” There are\nWomen | 48 (ZS\nno significant differences in these opinions\namong men and women, or Clinton supporters\nTrump voters\n47) ETE\nand Trump backers.\nClinton voters\naly [ee\nVoters say press has too much influence.\nNote: Don’t know responses not shown. Q46bb.\nVoters grade the press very negatively, and\nSource: Voter callback survey conducted Nov. 10-14, 2016.\nmost (57%) say it had too much influence on\nPRESSS SEs\nthe outcome of the election. Just 27% say the CT\npress had the right amount of influence on the election, while 13% say it had too little influence.\nAbout six-in-ten Trump voters (62%) say the press had too much influence, as do 50% of Clinton\nvoters.\nwww.pewresearch.org",
        "caption_result": "这张图片是**皮尤研究中心（Pew Research Center）**一份关于**2016年美国大选后选民态度**的调查报告页面。\n\n主要内容概括如下：\n*   **左侧文本**：列出了几项重要调查发现，包括选民对特朗普执政后**种族关系**的悲观预期、对**计票准确性**的信心变化、对**女性总统**的预期，以及认为**新闻媒体对选举影响力过大**的看法。\n*   **右侧图表**：是一个条形图，展示了不同群体（所有选民、男女、特朗普和克林顿支持者）对“**有生之年国家是否会选出女总统**”的预测。数据显示，绝大多数选民（约80%）对此持肯定态度。"
